    "media:imagetext": "THE HAWAII CLIPPER\nA Martin 130, No. NC 14715, shown in Hawaii\nat\nPearl Harbor, was assumed to have crashed in the\nPacific after leaving the Island of Guam in 1938.\nThe U.S.S. Penguin, a station ship at Guam, part-\nticipated in her search for many days. Never a\ntrace of her was found. To this day her disappear-\nance remains a mystery.\n0921\nPhoto courtesy of John L. Johnson, Jr.\nJ\u0026R A Guam Production\n310\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\nPOST CARD",
